      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DON'T TOUCH (1) has been burning up the tracks on the picnic circuits, and her form has also been solid at the tote meetings. She has plenty of natural pace, and over this suitable 870m trip, she can make it a hat-trick of wins. EYE WANTED (7) is a durable veteran mare, who hit her straps at the end of her 7YO season in late January, winning a brace at Kilcoy. She might need the run, but has trialled up twice to get fit, and she can't be taken lightly fresh. SCARTOON (8) finished third fresh up, and was less than a length from the winner. He only win came second up, and she has more upside than most in this. Stick with her. SILK SONIC (5) resumes from a spell, and if she can find the form that she showed earlier in her career, then she is capable of giving this a big shake, especially after a recent sound trial effort for second. KIRKSVILLE (2) is another fresh up local, and he looked in good condition when winning a recent Dalby trial. He is ready to rumble from a good gate.",
